cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "PlantLLPS and GrapeCondensatome"
message: "If you use this software or atlas, please cite the companion grapevine MAP/LLPS study and this resource."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Guan
    given-names: Pingyin
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0003-4890-3412"
    affiliation: "College of Horticulture, China Agricultural University, Beijing 100193, China"
version: "0.4.0"
date-released: "2026-11-26"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/pingyguan-glitch/grape-condensatome"
abstract: >-
  PlantLLPS is a plant-aware sequence scorer for liquid–liquid phase separation
  propensity. GrapeCondensatome is the PlantLLPS-scored UniProt UP000009183
  Vitis vinifera proteome atlas with confidence tiers and UniProt annotation joins.
keywords:
  - liquid-liquid phase separation
  - condensatome
  - Vitis vinifera
  - PlantLLPS
  - microtubule-associated proteins
preferred-citation:
  type: article
  title: "PlantLLPS: a plant-trained predictor of liquid–liquid phase separation and a grapevine whole-proteome condensatome atlas"
  authors:
    - family-names: Guan
      given-names: Pingyin
  notes: "Manuscript in preparation; cite this software release and the companion MAP/LLPS screen when available."
